---
Run these commands from the ZML checkout used in the
[quickstart]($link.page('zml/user-guide/quickstart')). Bazel selects and builds the target.
Each example executable defines its runtime arguments.
See [Environment variables]($link.page('zml/cli-reference/environment-variables'))
for model access and runtime settings.

# [List, build, run, and test targets]($heading.id('build-run-or-test-a-target'))

```=html
<div class="zml-command-index" role="list" aria-label="Bazel commands">
  <div class="zml-command-row" role="listitem">
    <div class="zml-command-task"><strong>List</strong><p>Find example target labels.</p></div>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy list command">bazel query '//examples/...'</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="zml-command-row" role="listitem">
    <div class="zml-command-task"><strong>Build</strong><p>Compile MNIST.</p></div>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy build command">bazel build //examples/mnist</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="zml-command-row" role="listitem">
    <div class="zml-command-task"><strong>Run</strong><p>Launch MNIST with its declared data and runtime files.</p></div>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy run command">bazel run //examples/mnist</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="zml-command-row" role="listitem">
    <div class="zml-command-task"><strong>Test</strong><p>Run the ZML framework tests.</p></div>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy test command">bazel test //zml:test</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
```

For complete workflows, see the recipes to
[run an LLM]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/build-and-run-with-bazel').ref('run-an-llm-example')),
[test ZML]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/build-and-run-with-bazel').ref('test-zml')),
[capture a trace]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/build-and-run-with-bazel').ref('profile-an-llm-example')), or
[package a build]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/build-and-run-with-bazel').ref('package-a-build-for-a-different-host')).
The [data-parallel MNIST example]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/run-across-devices').ref('run-data-parallel-mnist'))
distributes a batch of images across a device mesh.

# [Run an LLM example]($heading.id('run-an-llm-example'))

```=html
<div class="zml-command-boundary">
  <span class="command-language icon-code">Shell</span>
  <pre><code data-copy-label="Copy LLM help command"><span class="token function">bazel</span> run //examples/llm <mark>--</mark> --help</code></pre>
  <p><strong><code>--</code> separates the arguments.</strong> Place Bazel options before the target. After <code>--</code>, the executable receives <code>--help</code> and prints its own options.</p>
</div>
```

See [LLM example flags]($link.ref('llm-example-flags')) for model locations,
attention backends, and defaults.

# [Choose a backend and target platform]($heading.id('choose-a-backend-and-target-platform'))

Set a backend with `--@zml//platforms:<backend>=true`. Bazel includes the
runtime when the build target satisfies the backend's platform constraints.
Use the [MNIST backend picker]($link.page('zml/user-guide/quickstart').ref('build-and-run-mnist'))
for build and run commands on a compatible host.

| Backend | Bazel flag | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CPU | `--@zml//platforms:cpu` | `true` |
| NVIDIA CUDA | `--@zml//platforms:cuda` | `false` |
| AMD ROCm | `--@zml//platforms:rocm` | `false` |
| Intel oneAPI | `--@zml//platforms:oneapi` | `false` |
| Google TPU | `--@zml//platforms:tpu` | `false` |
| AWS Neuron | `--@zml//platforms:neuron` | `false` |
| Apple Metal | `--@zml//platforms:metal` | `false` |
| Furiosa | `--@zml//platforms:furiosa` | `false` |

Set `--platforms=@zml//platforms:linux_amd64` to target Linux x86-64. Other
labels with the same prefix are `linux_arm64`, `macos_amd64`, and
`macos_arm64`. Bazel uses the host platform by default for these commands
unless a configuration selects another target platform. Check
[Hardware compatibility]($link.page('zml/user-guide/reference/hardware-compatibility')) for backend and host
constraints before cross-building.

At runtime, `Platform.auto()` tries compiled-in backends in this order: TPU,
Neuron, ROCm, CUDA, oneAPI, Metal, Furiosa, then CPU. Check the platform
printed by the example. The LLM example's `--backend` option selects its
attention implementation within the chosen runtime.

# [LLM example flags]($heading.id('llm-example-flags'))

Omit `--prompt` for an interactive prompt, or pass `--model=/path/to/model`
for local weights. The example selects the implementation from `model_type`
in `config.json`. To serve a model over HTTP, [start an LLMD server]($link.page('llmd/user-guide/quickstart')).

| Example flag | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--model=<path>` | Required | Local model directory or `hf://`, `s3://`, or `gs://` URI. |
| `--prompt=<text>` | Unset | Generate a single response. |
| `--seqlen=<tokens>` | `2048` | Sequence length used for compilation and generation. |
| `--topk=<number>` | `4` | Top-k sampling cutoff for the example. |
| `--backend=<name>` | Automatic | Choose `stablehlo`, `cute`, `nki`, or `metal` attention on a compatible runtime. |
| `--profile` | Off | Capture a PJRT trace for a non-interactive run. |
| `-h`, `--help` | Off | Print the executable's help. |

# [Build and profiling configurations]($heading.id('select-a-build-or-profiling-configuration'))

| Bazel option | Default in this checkout | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--compilation_mode=<mode>` | `dbg` | Select the Bazel target compilation mode. The checkout configures Zig modes separately. |
| `--config=<name>` | Unset. Base `.bazelrc` settings apply. | Apply a named group of settings from `.bazelrc`. |
| `--run_under=<wrapper>` | Unset | Run a target through a wrapper, such as a profiler. |
| `--test_output=<mode>` | `errors` | Print test logs for failures. Use `all` when diagnosing a passing test. |

| Named profile | Scope | Effect when selected |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--config=debug` | Build, run, test | Use optimized Bazel compilation mode and debug mode for target Zig code. |
| `--config=alldebug` | Build, run, test | Use debug compilation mode, debug Zig mode, and local execution. |
| `--config=release` | Build, run, test | Use optimized compilation mode, Zig `release_safe`, and symbol stripping. |
| `--config=native` | Host-tuned builds | Tune code generation to the build machine. Omit this profile for portable artifacts. |
| `--config=silent` | Build, run, test | Reduce Bazel output. |
| `--config=nsys` | `bazel run` | Enable CUDA and wrap the executable with Nsight Systems. |
| `--config=rocprofv3` | `bazel run` | Enable ROCm and wrap the executable with ROCm's profiler. |
| `--config=neuron-profile` | `bazel run` | Enable Neuron, disable CPU, and invoke the Neuron profiling wrapper. |

See the [ZML Bazel configuration](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/.bazelrc)
and the [Bazel command reference](https://bazel.build/reference/command-line-reference).
